; g28.ngc - a slicer's G28 inside a program (end G-code parking):
;   o<g28> call [X] [Y] [Z]   1 = move that axis to its home position
; A program cannot home in LinuxCNC; the converter turns a G28 after the
; start G-code into this call. The positions are the INI's [UI_HOME].
; Z goes first when its home is above it (a CNC: clear the work), last
; when below (a printer: X/Y away from the print first).
o<g28> sub
#<zh> = #<_ini[UI_HOME]Z>
o<g28_zup> if [#3 GT 0 AND #<zh> GT #<_abs_z>]
  G53 G0 Z#<zh>
o<g28_zup> endif
o<g28_xy> if [#1 GT 0 AND #2 GT 0]
  G53 G0 X#<_ini[UI_HOME]X> Y#<_ini[UI_HOME]Y>
o<g28_xy> elseif [#1 GT 0]
  G53 G0 X#<_ini[UI_HOME]X>
o<g28_xy> elseif [#2 GT 0]
  G53 G0 Y#<_ini[UI_HOME]Y>
o<g28_xy> endif
o<g28_zdown> if [#3 GT 0 AND #<zh> LE #<_abs_z>]
  G53 G0 Z#<zh>
o<g28_zdown> endif
o<g28> endsub
M2
